kernel-grader-mi300x
Copyright 2026 Laela Zorana

Seven graded environments, each carrying a plain grader and a hardened one, and
the measurements that set their tolerances.

The kernel numbers were measured by Laela Zorana on an AMD Instinct MI300X VF,
gfx942, under ROCm 7.2.4. One global atomic per key measured 86.3898 ms and the
version privatised into local data share measured 0.1015 ms, a factor of 851.13,
on the same card in the same run.

The tolerance bound of 432 units in the last place comes from a measured worst
correct accumulation order of 108 on that card. The same bound was then carried
onto an AWS Trainium NeuronCore of a trn1.2xlarge, where 0 of 4096 bins went
over it at any of four seeds.

The per bin dataset in dataset/nki_bins.jsonl holds 16384 rows produced by those
two runs, one row per bin per seed, with the simulator value and the device
value side by side.

The three files under dataset/ are released under CC BY 4.0 rather than Apache 2.0, and carry their
own card in that folder.

